Sval: the menu bar's Workspaces, Favorites and Tab menus, without Work Offline, Page Style, Search History or the developer restart

The three menus start hidden in the markup, which every macOS window
includes, the hidden window among them: it shows its menu bar when no other
window is open, is created before Sval's startup code runs, and has no
workspace, favorite or tab to act on. macOS reads only `hidden` when it draws
the menu bar (`nsMenuUtilsX::NodeIsHiddenOrCollapsed`). `SvalMenuBar` shows
and fills them in each browser window.

Work Offline and Page Style go with everything that serves only them: the
`BrowserOffline` object and its command, `gPageStyleMenu` and its script, the
`PageStyle` actor, their strings and their tests. Gecko keeps
`Services.io.offline`, which it sets when the system loses the network and
which `navigator.onLine` reads, and the document viewer's
`authorStyleDisabled`. Search History and the History menu's other way into
the History sidebar, renamed Show History, open the same sidebar.

File's Restart (Developer) and its Accel+Alt+R key go with
`DevelopmentHelpers` and its script. Firefox adds them to any build
without MOZILLA_OFFICIAL, which Sval never sets (decision 0063), so every
Sval would otherwise ship a local build's restart shortcut.

